            {
                "entry_id": "c4bc5c0d-39f3-3d0b-83e4-25cade06ab8f",
                "word": "nonce",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ed3a8758-925f-4795-8e57-756b76bffb7c",
                        "entry_id": "c4bc5c0d-39f3-3d0b-83e4-25cade06ab8f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "nonces"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a3f99210-7938-3db8-b31f-a4d575069650",
                        "entry_id": "c4bc5c0d-39f3-3d0b-83e4-25cade06ab8f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nombre arbitraire, à usage unique, utilisé pour signer un ensemble de données d’une communication électronique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "60787f07-7e06-4e64-83c9-4d5111fd5173",
                                "sense_id": "a3f99210-7938-3db8-b31f-a4d575069650",
                                "text": "En simpliste : le boulot d'un miner c'est de prendre ton block actuel et d'y ajouter un nombre calculé appelé nonce pour ensuite en calculer le hash (en SHA-256 pour bitcoin), ça te sortira un nombre, si ton nombre est en dessous du chiffre target = tu win le bloc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78e3ff43-ac73-4252-aec5-c0608c5630c8",
                                "sense_id": "a3f99210-7938-3db8-b31f-a4d575069650",
                                "text": "Les utilisateurs et les contrats ont des adresses Ethereum, fabriquées à partir de l’adresse du créateur du contrat et du nonce ayant validé la transaction."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4ecf77b6-e73c-4003-994d-0836c6b0dab5",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4bc5c0d-39f3-3d0b-83e4-25cade06ab8f",
                        "source_sense_id": "a3f99210-7938-3db8-b31f-a4d575069650",
                        "source_sense_description": "Nombre arbitraire",
                        "target_lang_word": "nonce",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nonce",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0ab537d4-91be-37da-9d73-4b0a1d3c4f96",
                                        "entry_id": "9a8bb0c6-60ef-34cb-884e-f253c71bcb4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The one or single occasion; the present reason or purpose (now only in for the nonce)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0413930-d1fb-45cc-84f5-3fcee3d007d6",
                                                "sense_id": "0ab537d4-91be-37da-9d73-4b0a1d3c4f96",
                                                "text": "[...] Dunce, / Dotard, a-dozing at the very nonce, / After a life spent training for the sight!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7bb65b5-6985-4994-a3ac-a4a7b4afcb4b",
                                                "sense_id": "0ab537d4-91be-37da-9d73-4b0a1d3c4f96",
                                                "text": "That will do for the nonce, but we'll need a better answer for the long term."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca1247ab-931e-416e-ae99-2600dd4d44b4",
                                                "sense_id": "0ab537d4-91be-37da-9d73-4b0a1d3c4f96",
                                                "text": "'Idiot!' exclaimed the doctor, who for the nonce was not capable of more than such spasmodic attempts at utterance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9723ce01-e135-32ba-8229-60a0a60f48e9",
                                        "entry_id": "9a8bb0c6-60ef-34cb-884e-f253c71bcb4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A nonce word."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d5f8968-e86e-4cb0-8ab1-e9dc098183df",
                                                "sense_id": "9723ce01-e135-32ba-8229-60a0a60f48e9",
                                                "text": "I had thought that the term was a nonce, but it seems as if it's been picked up by other authors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "266b7bc3-e7d9-3983-b22c-f56e47ecd7d6",
                                        "entry_id": "9a8bb0c6-60ef-34cb-884e-f253c71bcb4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A value constructed so as to be unique to a particular message in a stream, in order to prevent replay attacks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cb306aa-e226-498d-ba3d-61e46075a5cc",
                                                "sense_id": "266b7bc3-e7d9-3983-b22c-f56e47ecd7d6",
                                                "text": "The protocol opens with A communicating in clear to AS his own claimed identity and the identity of the desired correspondent, B, together with A's nonce identifier for this transaction, I_(A1). (\"Nonce\" means \"used only once.\")"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b750320a-c619-4e99-aa5e-29cc5deb3372",
                                                "sense_id": "266b7bc3-e7d9-3983-b22c-f56e47ecd7d6",
                                                "text": "The information gained by the eavesdropper would permit a replay attack, but only with a request for the same document, and even that may be limited by the server's choice of nonce."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bab19bbd-9591-4ee2-bd05-561d8e5fca50",
                                                "sense_id": "266b7bc3-e7d9-3983-b22c-f56e47ecd7d6",
                                                "text": "Both CCM and GCM require a unique nonce (N used once) value to maintain their privacy and authenticity goals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5197926-ad1e-478f-80d0-99072252712c",
                                                "sense_id": "266b7bc3-e7d9-3983-b22c-f56e47ecd7d6",
                                                "text": "The main idea with the challenge-response type of authentication protocol is that the challenge sent by the server is used only once (referred to as a cryptographic nonce, which means “number used once”)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "nonce",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5e1c887-290d-3153-b0e2-466ba79837a9",
                                        "entry_id": "935185c4-a73b-39e9-b4e1-2e09cf572916",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One-off; produced or created for a single occasion or use. Denoting something occurring once."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "739aa5a4-a291-4d81-a881-04527bb2d591",
                                                "sense_id": "b5e1c887-290d-3153-b0e2-466ba79837a9",
                                                "text": "But particular men are not stereotyped for jobs nor particular desks (as against others) to sit at - the standard here is nonce."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2677463-9d85-467d-9cab-bdbb8dce2e40",
                                                "sense_id": "b5e1c887-290d-3153-b0e2-466ba79837a9",
                                                "text": "Dickinson's association of heliotrope with Mary Bowles was nonce and fleeting, but the subject of gardens was always a safe one on which to address her: “How is your garden – Mary? Are the Pinks true –?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5b25cae-d4c9-4cf3-89a1-f405bc940d90",
                                                "sense_id": "b5e1c887-290d-3153-b0e2-466ba79837a9",
                                                "text": "Poplack et al. (1988, 57) found that 65% of their types were nonce and only 7% of the types were considered widespread."
                                            },
                                            {
